  "text": "That sounds like a wonderful idea! A classic breakfast omelette is a comforting and delicious way to show your mom you care. Here's a simple and reliable recipe for a classic breakfast omelette that's easy to make and guaranteed to please:\n\n---\n\n### \ud83c\udf73 Classic Breakfast Omelette Recipe\n\n**Ingredients:**\n\n- 2 large eggs\n- 1/4 cup of milk or cream (optional, for fluffiness)\n- Salt and pepper to taste\n- 1/2 teaspoon of butter or oil (for cooking)\n- Optional fillings:\n  - Saut\u00e9ed spinach or mushrooms\n  - Chopped cheese (like cheddar, Swiss, or mozzarella)\n  - Sliced ham or bacon\n  - Fresh herbs (like parsley or dill)\n  - A sprinkle of paprika or hot sauce (for a bit of kick)\n\n**Instructions:**\n\n1. **Whisk the eggs:** In a medium bowl, whisk the eggs with the milk or cream (if using), salt, and pepper until well combined.\n\n2. **Heat the pan:** In a non-stick skillet over medium heat, add the butter or oil. Let it melt and coat the bottom of the pan.\n\n3. **Cook the eggs:** Pour the egg mixture into the pan. Let it sit for about 30 seconds, then gently stir with a spatula to loosen the edges. Cook for 1\u20132 minutes until the eggs are just set but still soft in the center.\n\n4. **Add fillings:** While the eggs are still slightly runny, add your chosen fillings (like cheese, spinach, ham, etc.). Fold the omelette in half or crimp the edges to enclose the fillings.\n\n5. **Finish cooking:** Cook for another 1\u20132 minutes, or until the omelette is fully cooked and golden.\n\n6. **Serve:** Slide the omelette onto a plate, and serve immediately with toast, fresh fruit, or a side of breakfast potatoes if desired.\n\n---\n\n### \ud83c\udf81 Surprise Tips for Mother\u2019s Day:\n\n- Make it extra special by adding a small handwritten note in a card.\n- Pair the omelette with a fresh flower or a small gift, like a candle or a book she loves.\n- Clean up quickly \u2014 you don\u2019t want to wake your mom up with a mess!\n\nLet me know if you want a version with cheese, vegetables, or even a sweet twist like chocolate! \ud83d\ude0a",
